<title>USA: Pen Interconnect Inc Q2 net earnings rise.</title>
<headline>Pen Interconnect Inc Q2 net earnings rise.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(amounts in thousands except per share)</p>
<p>			Three months ended	  Six months ended</p>
<p>			     March 31		     March 31</p>
<p>			   1997	1996	     1997	1996</p>
<p> Net sales	  $5,482.3 $5,442.1	 $10,740.6 $10,012.6</p>
<p>Net earnings from</p>
<p>  operations	   101.9     71.7	     164.3     251.9</p>
<p>Net earning from</p>
<p>  sale of division				    367.1</p>
<p> Total net earnings  101.9     71.7	     531.4     251.9</p>
<p>Net earnings per</p>
<p>  share		   0.03     0.03		0.18	0.10</p>
<p>Average number of</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>			 3,033.4  2,700.0	   3,033.4   2,450.0</p>
<p>Notes: The company said its rise in Q2 net earnings is the result of cost reductions in Q1 and Q2. The 110 percent rise in six-month net earnings is largely the result of the sale of a division in Q1.</p>
</text>
